                <pb facs="0230" n="134" sameAs="frus:frus1879/pg134"/>

                <head>No. 72.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. White
                        to Mr. Evarts.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >United States Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Rio de
                                Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1879-03-25"><hi rendition="#italic">March</hi> 25, 1879</date>.
                        (Received April 28.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 81.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In my No. 65 I referred to the importance
                    of having <hi rendition="#italic">solid</hi> American business houses
                    established here.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">* * * * * * *</p>
                <pb facs="0231" n="135" xml:id="pg135"/>
                <p>The great bulk of our goods are handled by foreign dealers who take them because
                    they are forced to. A new element is needed here, a stronger national prestige
                    must be impressed upon the markets. It is necessary that the merchants and
                    manufacturers doing business with Brazil should be represented here. Selling by
                    sample and consigning to commission houses of very limited capital will not
                    bring about the equality of the exports and imports. We need here the real
                    American reliability coupled with energy and sustained by financial strength. If
                    some distinguished merchant (Hon. Elliot C. Cowdin, for instance) could be
                    induced to visit Brazil he would impart more information and give better advice
                    than could be crowded into one hundred dispatches.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>JOHN C. WHITE.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
